WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.200
There is currently a Senator Kennedy in the Senate&nbsp;
and he's actually named John Kennedy, but he's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:13.840
Republican. He is not related to the well-known&nbsp;
Kennedys of of Democratic Party fame. And in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.360
wake of multiple major mass shootings in the last&nbsp;
week, Senator Kennedy has been doing the rounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:27.120
to equate guns to cars, insisting that, listen,&nbsp;
we don't ban cars because sometimes people die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:33.920
in car accidents. We don't ban cars because&nbsp;
sometimes people drive drunk. And this could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.200
not be a sillier analogy. And we're going to talk&nbsp;
about why in a moment. But understand that at a at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.040
a top level, even comparing cars and guns is&nbsp;
fraught because of their intended purposes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.200
Cars were never designed to kill&nbsp;
people or animals or maim them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:55.840
Yes, a car can be misused as a weapon, but it&nbsp;
wasn't invented for that. Guns were invented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:03.680
to kill or maim people or animals and sometimes&nbsp;
to threaten people with the fear of doing that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.160
Yes, guns can be used for target practice.&nbsp;
That's not what they were invented for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:14.800
Most people don't own guns merely for target&nbsp;
practice. Most car related deaths are accidents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:21.520
Most gun related deaths are deliberate homicides&nbsp;
and suicides. There are gun accidents as well. OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.800
so the comparison at a base level makes no&nbsp;
sense. Senator John Kennedy and some others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.080
don't care or don't know. Here is John Kennedy at&nbsp;
a congressional hearing earlier this week saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.880
we have lots of drunk driving deaths.&nbsp;
We don't ban sober drivers from driving.&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.840
But I do think we ought to&nbsp;
keep this in perspective.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:49.920
What has happened in the last few days, what's&nbsp;
happened in the last years is, of course, tragic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.920
And I'm not I'm not trying to&nbsp;
perfectly equate these two, but.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.760
We have a lot of drunk drivers in&nbsp;
America that kill a lot of people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:13.440
We are well to try to combat that, too.&nbsp;
But I think what many folks on my side of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.760
the aisle are saying is that the answer&nbsp;
is not to get rid of all sober drivers.&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.960
The answers to concentrate on the problem,&nbsp;
I guess Senator Kennedy really liked this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:31.440
analogy because then he appeared on Fox News&nbsp;
and made a similar car related analogy to guns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.720
during an interview with Fox and Friends&nbsp;
host Brian Kilmeade yesterday morning.&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:45.920
But you don't stop drunk drivers getting rid&nbsp;
of all sober drivers, which is what many of my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:51.600
Democratic friends want to do with respect to the&nbsp;
Second Amendment and my judgment. We do not need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:57.920
more gun control. We need more idiot control.
So part of the problem with saying that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:04.880
is about idiot control, so therefore don't do&nbsp;
anything about guns is that it's too easy for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.520
idiots in the U.S. to get guns in the first place&nbsp;
and there's too many idiots in the United States.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:17.680
But the analogy to vehicles is really a terrible&nbsp;
one because we already regulate vehicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.360
way more than we regulate getting guns.&nbsp;
John Kennedy says let's not go crazy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:30.640
with cars like some want to do with guns because&nbsp;
that would be bad. Actually, we do much more with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.680
drivers and vehicles already to get a driver's&nbsp;
license in the first place. In most states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.280
you need to pass a written test, have a certain&nbsp;
number of practice hours, pass a driving test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.960
renew the license periodically. Sometimes that&nbsp;
includes an eye exam. If you get too many tickets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.120
you lose your license. If you don't pay tickets,&nbsp;
you can lose your license. In most states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.400
the car has to be insured. In most states you&nbsp;
need to have the car inspected yearly for safety.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:02.000
Depending on the age of the car, there would be an&nbsp;
emissions test to see if it's roadworthy based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.400
modern emission standards. If you drive drunk,&nbsp;
you can use your license or even go to prison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:14.560
It's not. You know, no one is suggesting. He&nbsp;
says, let's not do with cars what we do with what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:20.000
Democrats want to do with guns. In reality, it's&nbsp;
Republicans who don't even want to do with guns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:25.440
what we already do with cars and drivers. I have&nbsp;
many Democratic and left leaning friends who own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:32.000
firearms. They all want universal background&nbsp;
checks, mandatory waiting period to get a gun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:38.080
limits on certain types of weapons, but arguably,&nbsp;
just as importantly, limits on certain ammunition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:44.640
purchases, mandatory relicensing and&nbsp;
testing and mandatory gun insurance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:50.080
We have a Second Amendment. I'm not disputing&nbsp;
that. None of my left leaning gun owner friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:56.240
are disputing that. What we're disputing is that&nbsp;
we don't even make it as difficult to get a gun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:03.040
as we make it to get a driver's license. And&nbsp;
that doesn't make any sense whatsoever. And a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:09.440
lot of this stuff is actually not controversial.&nbsp;
Universal background checks. You know, it ebbs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.320
flows over time, but it's overwhelmingly popular&nbsp;
with the American people. In the wake of the Sandy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:18.480
Hook shooting, it was like eighty eight to 90&nbsp;
percent support. Republicans just said no, it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:24.960
a nonstarter with Republicans. A lot of this isn't&nbsp;
controversial with the American people. And it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:31.040
a designed controversy by the NRA and other groups&nbsp;
because they just want to sell guns. Always the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:36.080
threat of someone taking your gun is a great way&nbsp;
to get people to go and buy guns before they make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:43.280
them illegal. Right. This is this is how the NRA&nbsp;
sells guns. And from the standpoint of elections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:50.160
these are often for the right great issues for&nbsp;
raising money. So terrible analogy. Cars and&nbsp;&nbsp;

